WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.593
A full-set offer waits for all configured tier
targets, rather than discounting any two unrelated

2
00:00:05.593 --> 00:00:11.931
products. In this example, Coral is the starting
product and Sun is the required second product. We

3
00:00:11.931 --> 00:00:18.642
will configure ten percent for the trigger and twenty
percent for Sun. Choose Tiered discount, name the test

4
00:00:18.642 --> 00:00:24.981
and use percentage rewards. Keep this as a separate
draft instead of editing an existing live campaign.

5
00:00:26.031 --> 00:00:33.217
In Conditions, choose Products or variants and select
Coral. Turn on Apply only when full set is in cart.

6
00:00:33.217 --> 00:00:39.269
This controls eligibility. Apply discount to trigger
products is a separate decision: enable it and enter

7
00:00:39.269 --> 00:00:45.321
ten percent only because this example includes a
reward for Coral itself. Leaving that second switch

8
00:00:45.321 --> 00:00:50.616
off would not give Coral its own discount. Neither
switch selects Sun for you.

9
00:00:51.666 --> 00:00:58.033
In Rewards, enter twenty percent for Tier Two and
select Sun under Required Products for This Tier.

10
00:00:58.033 --> 00:01:05.149
Check the returned product card. Leaving an optional
target list empty can broaden the rule, so do not skip

11
00:01:05.149 --> 00:01:10.392
this selection. Review the complete-set requirement,
separate trigger rate and Sun reward together, then

12
00:01:10.392 --> 00:01:14.886
save inactive. Reopen both steps to confirm these
values survived the save.

13
00:01:15.936 --> 00:01:21.580
This video proves the stored configuration, not a
newly activated checkout calculation. Before

14
00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:28.526
launching, test Coral alone, Sun alone, both together
and removal of either required item. With one

15
00:01:28.526 --> 00:01:34.604
twenty-four-dollar Coral at ten percent and one
twelve-dollar Sun at twenty percent, the illustrative

16
00:01:34.604 --> 00:01:41.116
merchandise total is thirty-one dollars and twenty
cents, before tax, shipping and other discounts. Also

17
00:01:41.116 --> 00:01:48.931
test repeated units and two complete sets; never infer
the result from the number of visible cart rows.
